sieve-filter-v2
; melody-lengths-v1 on every note set (notes104 and notes2): note and rest lengths from `shortest`
; to `longest`, and at most `eighths` quick events (an eighth long or shorter: s, e) in a row. The
; lengths are the real ones, in sixteenths (LENGTH, SIXTEENTHS), so a set's durations are judged by
; how long they are, not by their place in it. On notes104 it is exactly melody-lengths-v1.
id        melody-lengths
version   2
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes*
describe  Note lengths from shortest to longest, and at most so many eighths (or shorter) in a row, on every note set.
param     shortest  choice  s s,e,E,q,Q,h,H,w the shortest note or rest allowed
param     longest   choice  w s,e,E,q,Q,h,H,w the longest note or rest allowed
param     eighths   int     2  0  32  the most notes or rests of an eighth or shorter in a row

states    {eighths + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{eighths}
for s 0 {eighths}
  for p 0 {PITCHES}
    for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
      if {LENGTH(d) >= SIXTEENTHS(shortest) && LENGTH(d) <= SIXTEENTHS(longest)}
        if {LENGTH(d) <= 2}
          if {s < eighths}
            t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} {s + 1}
          fi
        else
          t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} 0
        fi
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
